            <div xml:id="d817">

                <pb facs="1049" n="947" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg947"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.01 Foreign Control/950a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Liberia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hibbard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-06-03T13:00:00-04:00">June 3, 1935—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8. We gather from your telegrams that the Liberian Congress is now in session;
                    please telegraph us briefly as to the prospects for early repeal of the
                    repudiationist legislation.</p>
                <p>For your information. The British Government has informed us that they do not
                    feel justified in recognizing the Barclay régime until the final settlement of
                    the Kru problem. We have decided, however, not to delay our recognition further
                    and the President has approved our recommendations for the recognition of the
                    Barclay régime shortly after the Liberian Legislature has repealed the
                    legislation in question; he is also prepared to designate McCaskey as Financial
                    Adviser.</p>
                <p>You should make discreet use of the foregoing only in case there is some hitch in
                    the legislature which has not been foreseen.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
